// "Draw N" ([CR#121.1]): the imperative you-form draw — you draw N cards,
// one at a time ([CR#121.2] — a per-card sequence, not a simultaneous batch
// like mill). A `Batch(N, ...)` over the per-unit `DrawCard(You)`. The
// `Batch` gives a count-doubling replacement (Alhammarret's Archive,
// [CR#121.2a,616.1g]) one aggregate window; the engine then runs the N
// contained draws sequentially — each binds the library top late and
// empty-checks before its move, so an empty library loses the game
// ([CR#121.4,104.3c]).
//
// NOT a keyword action, and NOT a `Composite`: [CR#701] enumerates the
// keyword actions and drawing is not among them — it is [CR#121], a game
// action. Drawing is also irreducible, so there is no body to store:
// [CR#121.5] states that a library -> Hand move made without the word
// "draw" is not a draw, so such a body would denote a different event. The
// performer rides `DrawCard`'s own agent slot — same position, but distinct
// arity+type from this macro's own `Count` argument, so `DrawCard(You)` the
// variant and `Draw(1)` the macro invocation never collide. (This macro
// keeps the `KeywordAction` macro kind: that kind is the English verb
// registry — the conjugation data the renderer needs — not a [CR#701]
// claim. See `Mill.ron` for a body that is its verb's meaning.)
//
// The declarative-subject form ("Target player draws N cards.") is the
// `Draws(who, n)` macro; this is the bare you-imperative.
//
// Usage: Draw(1) -> "Draw a card." / Draw(3) -> "Draw three cards."
(
    name: "Draw",
    template: "draw ${0:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect, KeywordAction],
    params: [Count],
    // The checked-in `template:` uses the `card|cards` pluralization codec,
    // which the legacy `template:` mini-language cannot express as a
    // projection of frame text — so this def is reported excepted, not
    // divergent, regardless of this frame's exact wording. "cards" is
    // picked over "card" arbitrarily.
    //
    // Second frame: `Count`'s `Numeral` hole only ever matches a *quantity*
    // determiner ("N cards") — the legacy `${0:card|cards}` codec's `n == 1`
    // case ("a card", an *indefinite*-determiner nominal, a structurally
    // different tree) needs its own zero-hole literal frame.
    //
    // Guarded on the bare canonical spelling `"1"`, not `"Literal(1)"`: a
    // `Count` literal serializes bare and the `Literal(…)` wrapper never
    // appears in real RON (`crates/deckmaste_core/src/count.rs`'s own doc)
    // — canon authors write `Draw(1)`, not `Draw(Literal(1))`. Guard
    // comparison normalizes either spelling to the same value, but the
    // canonical one is what a reader expects alongside real corpus RON.
    frames: [
        "draw <Param(0)> cards",
        (text: "draw a card", when: [(0, "1")]),
    ],
    body: Batch(Param(0), DrawCard(You)),
)
